{
 "_note": "What makes a question a question about drugs, for Insight's last line when it has no answer (site 2.5, 15 November 2026; the senior author, of \"can i die from mosquito bites\" being offered \"Ask us to check it\": \"pharmakon insight should understand trolling ... this is a drug website there should be no mistakes\"). A question is taken as being about drugs when it names a drug the site covers (the index's names), or holds one of these: 'words' (drug talk: patterns, each between word boundaries, case ignored), 'names' (drugs and medicines the site does not cover yet: plain names), 'chem' (a research chemical's name by its shape, such as 6-APB or 4-AcO-DMT). 'not' are phrases taken out first, because in them a drug's name is not a drug (stomach acid, diet coke, cooking mushrooms). The rule is words only, no model: it is the same on the page and in the build (scripts/insight/build_index.py puts it into the index), and it is measured there (--eval) on the forum questions of the gold set and on data/verification/insight/scope-other.json. It decides one thing only: whether the page says \"We haven't checked exactly this yet\" with the way to ask us, or \"We have no answer to this. Pharmakon answers questions about drugs\" with a quiet way to send it all the same. Measured on 15 November 2026 (build_index.py --eval prints it at every build with --eval): of the 400 forum questions of the gold set the first version took 389 as drug questions, and of 635 other forum questions it had never seen, 597 (94 in 100); what those misses showed was then added, after which it takes 1,029 of the 1,035 (the same questions, so that is not a fresh measure); of 165 questions that are not about drugs it takes none as a drug question. A drug question it misses loses nothing: the line it gets is true for any question and keeps the way to send it, and the scout lists every question sent that way, which is how the list of words grows. Whether the site holds near answers was measured as a second sign and left out: it rescued 2 of the 6 misses and let in 11 of the 165. Every pattern must read the same in JavaScript and in Python (no \\p classes, no lookbehind).",
